0101           JOB  SCIP-SCREEN CARD INPUT TO CAPR SYSTEM - APR 22, 1966   SCIP3
AA02           CTL  431  1                                                 SCIP3
0103 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0104 *  PROGRAMMERS - DON MILLER AND DONNA MONTGOMERY                      SCIP3
0105 *                                                                     SCIP3
0106 *                                                                     SCIP3
0107 * A BRIEF SUMMARY OF THE PROGRAM                                      SCIP3
0108 *                                                                     SCIP3
0109 *     THIS PROGRAM ACCEPTS CARD IMAGE RECORDS IN THE FORM OF CARD     SCIP3
0110 * OR TAPE 1 INPUT.                                                    SCIP3
0111 *     IT PROCESSES THESE CARD IMAGES ONE AT A TIME EDITING ANY        SCIP3
0112 * REQUIRED FIELDS.  IF ALL FIELDS IN THE CARD IMAGE PASS THE EDIT,    SCIP3
0113 * THE RECORD IS MOVED INTO THE SPECIFIC AREA OF THE OUTPUT RECORD     SCIP3
0114 * DICTATED BY THE CARD CODE.                                          SCIP3
0115 *     HOWEVER, THE OUTPUT RECORD IS NEITHER WRITTEN ON TAPE 2 AS A    SCIP3
0116 * GOOD RECORD OR REJECTED UNTIL ANOTHER PROGRAM ID CARD IMAGE INPUT   SCIP3
0117 * IS RECEIVED OR AN ABSTRACT CARD IMAGE INPUT FOR THE SAME PROGRAM    SCIP3
0118 * ID.                                                                 SCIP3
0119 *     THE OUTPUT RECORD IS REJECTED FOR A PROGRAM ID FOR 5 REASONS-   SCIP3
0120 *         1. IF ANY FIELD FAILED TO PASS THE EDIT.                    SCIP3
0121 *         2. IF ANY NON IDENTICAL DUPLICATES  WERE RECEIVED- OTHER    SCIP3
0122 *           THAN ABSTRACTS. THE PROGRAM ACCEPTS THE FIRST RECORD      SCIP3
0123 *           IN THE CASE OF A DUPLICATE ABSTRACT INPUT.                SCIP3
0124 *         3. THE PROGRAM WILL REJECT ANY COMBINATION OF THE 4 TYPES   SCIP3
0125 *           OF INPUT PACKAGES.                                        SCIP3
0126 *         4. IF THE CHANGE DATA CARDS RECEIVED  DO  NOT AGREE WITH    SCIP3
0127 *           CHANGE CONTROL CARD.                                      SCIP3
0128 *         5. IF ADDITION PACKAGE DOES NOT INCLUDE AT LEAST ONE        SCIP3
0129 *            ABSTRACT CARD, PLUS ONE EACH A THRU 0 CARD.              SCIP3
0130 *                                                                     SCIP3
0131 *     THE INPUT CAN BE A COMBINATION OF CONTROL CARDS AND DATA        SCIP3
0132 *CARDS, IN SEQUENCE AS FOLLOWS-                                       SCIP3
0133 *         MAJOR-PROGRAM ID - COLS 1-8                                 SCIP3
0134 *         MINOR-CARD CODE  - COLS 9-10                                SCIP3
0135 *                                                                     SCIP3
0136 *     THERE ARE FOURS TYPES OF INPUT PACKAGES-                        SCIP3
0137 *         1. DELETE - A SINGLE CONTROL CARD.                          SCIP3
0138 *         2. INACTIVE- A SINGLE CONTROL CARD.                         SCIP3
0139 *         3. CHANGE- A SINGLE CONTROL CARD FOLLOWED BY THE DATA       SCIP3
0140 *            CARDS REQUIRED TO AFFECT THE CHANGE.  THE CHANGE         SCIP3
0141 *            CONTROL CARD WILL BE PUNCHED TO SHOW WHICH DATA          SCIP3
0142 *            CARDS MAY FOLLOW IT.  ABSTRACT CARDS MAY NOT BE          SCIP3
0143 *            INCLUDED.                                                SCIP3
0144 *              IF AN ABSTRACT NEEDS TO BE CHANGED THE ENTIRE          SCIP3
0145 *            PACKAGE SHOULD BE RESUBMITTED AS AN ADDITION. THE        SCIP3
0146 *            NEXT PROGRAM WILL RECOGNIZE IT AS A REPLACEMENT IF       SCIP3
0147 *            ANOTHER RECORD ALREADY EXISTS ON THE MASTER FILE.        SCIP3
0148 *         4. ADDITION- A COMPLETE SET OF DATA CARDS INCLUDING         SCIP3
0149 *            ABSTRACTS.                                               SCIP3
0150 *                                                                     SCIP3
0151 *ACCEPTABLE INPUT CARD CODES-                                         SCIP3
0152 *   COLS 9-10    COL 12  TYPE                                         SCIP3
0153 *     BLANKS         D   DELETE CONTROL                               SCIP3
0154 *     BLANKS         I   INACTIVE CONTROL                             SCIP3
0155 *     BLANKS         M   CHANGE-MODIFY CONTROL                        SCIP3
0156 *     A+BLANK            OTHER THAN ABSTRACT INFORMATION              SCIP3
0157 *     B+BLANK                                                         SCIP3
0158 *     C+BLANK                                                         SCIP3
0159 *     D+BLANK                                                         SCIP3
0160 *     S+BLANK                                                         SCIP3
0161 *     0+BLANK                                                         SCIP3
0162 *     10 THRU 99         ABSTRACT INFORMATION                         SCIP3
0163 *                                                                     SCIP3
0164 * SENSE SWICHES                                                       SCIP3
0165 *     IO- ALWAYS ON.                                                  SCIP3
0166 *     A - LAST CARD-ALWAYS ON.                                        SCIP3
0167 *     B - ON FOR CARD INPUT.                                          SCIP3
0168 *         OFF FOR TAPE INPUT.                                         SCIP3
0169 *     C - ON AT HALT 502 TO INDICATE NO MORE TAPE INPUT.              SCIP3
0170 *     D -IF THIS SWITCH IS ON, THE PROGRAM WILL BYPASS THE C CARD     SCIP3
0170A*         AUDIT OF DOCUMENTATION AVAILABLE.                           SCIP3
0170B*                                                                     SCIP3
0170C*         IF THIS SWITCH IS OFF, AN AUDIT OF THESE FIELDS WILL BE     SCIP3
0170D*         MADE, AS FOLLOWS - CARD COLUMNS 45-49 AND 50-54 MUST BE     SCIP3
0170E*         BLANK, OR THE FIRST 2 POSITIONS OF THE NON BLANK FIELD      SCIP3
0170F*         MUST BE ALPHABETIC.                                         SCIP3
0170G*         CARD COLUMNS 40-41 MUST BE ALPHA AND 42-44 MUST NOT BE      SCIP3
0170H*         BLANK.                                                      SCIP3
0171 *     E - IF THIS SWITCH IS ON, THE PROGRAM WILL BYPASS THE SHARE     SCIP3
0172 *         SUBJECT CODE FORMAT EDITING.  THE ONLY CHECKING DONE WILL   SCIP3
0173 *         BE ON THE PRIMARY SUBJECT CODE, WHICH MUST BE NON BLANK.    SCIP3
0174 *                                                                     SCIP3
0175 *         IF THIS SWITCH IS OFF, THE PROGRAM WILL PERFORM THE         SCIP3
0176 *         SHARE SUBJECT CODE FORMAT EDITING, AS FOLLOWS-              SCIP3
0177 *           1. PRIMARY CODE MUST BE NON BLANK.                        SCIP3
0178 *           2. SECONDARY CODES NEED NOT BE PUNCHED.                   SCIP3
0179 *           3. THE FORMAT RULES ARE-                                  SCIP3
0180 *              A. 1ST POSITION MUST BE ALPHABETIC.                    SCIP3
0181 *              B. 2ND POSITION MUST BE NUMERIC.                       SCIP3
0182 *              C. 3RD POSITION MUST BE BLANK.                         SCIP3
0183 *     F - IF THIS SWITCH IS ON THE PROGRAM WILL BYPASS THE SDA NO.    SCIP3
0184 *         CHECK, COLS. 13-19 OF THE A CARD.                           SCIP3
0185 *            ON- TO PROCESS SUBMITTALS FOR CHECK PRIOR TO SENDING     SCIP3
0186 *                THEM TO SDA - SDA NO. WILL BE MISSING                SCIP3
0187 *            OFF-TO PROCESS SUBMITTALS RECEIVED FROM SDA - MUST       SCIP3
0188 *                HAVE SDA NO. ASSIGNED AND PUNCHED.                   SCIP3
0189 *     G - THIS SWITCH IS USED TO RESPOND TO HALT 682.                 SCIP3
0190 *         THE HALT INDICATES THAT THE PROGRAM HAS TRIED 8 TIMES TO    SCIP3
0191 *         WRITE A TRAILER LABEL BUT THE ERROR CONDITION STILL         SCIP3
0192 *         PERSISTS.  THE  OPTIONS AVAILABLE  ARE-                     SCIP3
0193 *         1- SW G ON AND PRESS START TO BYPASS TRAILER WRITE AND      SCIP3
0194 *            WRITE 2ND TM INSTEAD.                                    SCIP3
0195 *         2- SW G OFF AND PRESS START TO SKIP AND BLANK TAPE AND      SCIP3
0196 *            TRY 8 MORE TIMES.                                        SCIP3
0197 *                                                                     SCIP3
0198 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0199 * HALTS AND ACTIONS                                                   SCIP3
0200 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0201 *                                                                     SCIP3
0202 *     HALT PROG.  CAUSE AND+OR                                        SCIP3
0203 *     NO.  LABEL  ACTION TO TAKE                                      SCIP3
0204 *     ---- -----  --------------                                      SCIP3
0205 *     501  I06    TAPE 1 READ ERROR.  PROGRAM HAS TRIED 9 TIMES TO    SCIP3
0206 *                 READ THE RECORD.                                    SCIP3
0207 *                 2 ACTION ALTERNATIVES-                              SCIP3
0208 *                   1. PRESS START TO TRY 9 MORE TIMES.               SCIP3
0209 *                   2. TAKE DIAGNOSTIC ACTION AND ABANDON JOB.        SCIP3
0210 *     502  I04Q   END OF REEL- TAPE 1 INPUT.                          SCIP3
0211 *                 2 ACTION ALTERNATIVES-                              SCIP3
0212 *                   1. IF NO MORE INPUT SET SENSE SW C ON AND PRESS   SCIP3
0213 *                      START TO GO TO END OF JOB.                     SCIP3
0214 *                   2. IF MORE INPUT MOUNT NEXT INPUT REEL, SET       SCIP3
0215 *                      SENSE SW C OFF AND PRESS START TO CONTINUE     SCIP3
0216 *                      PROCESSING.                                    SCIP3
0217 *     503  W05    END OF REEL ON OUTPUT TAPE 2.                       SCIP3
0218 *                 MOUNT SCRATCH AND PRESS START.                      SCIP3
0219 *     592  W10J4  PROGRAM TRYING TO WRITE HEADER LABEL ON OUTPUT      SCIP3
0220 *                 TAPE 2 BUT ERROR CONDITION PERSISTS.                SCIP3
0221 *                 MOUNT ANOTHER SCRATCH TAPE ON DRIVE 2 AND           SCIP3
0222 *                 PRESS START.                                        SCIP3
0223 *     600  I98B  INPUT OUT OF SEQUENCE ON COLUMNS 1-10.               SCIP3
0224 *                1. IF CARD INPUT, MARK THE SPOT IN THE CARD FILE     SCIP3
0225 *                   TO SHOW APPROXIMATE LOCATION OF OUT OF SEQUENCE   SCIP3
0226 *                   AND PRESS START TO CONTINUE PROCESSING.           SCIP3
0227 *                     NOTE -- AN OUTPUT TAPE PRODUCED BY A RUN        SCIP3
0228 *                             WHICH REACHED A HALT 600 IS IMPROPER    SCIP3
0229 *                             AND MUST BE SCRATCHED AT END OF JOB.    SCIP3
0230 *                              THE END OF JOB ROUTINE WILL BE AWARE   SCIP3
0231 *                             OF THIS CONDITION AND WILL REWIND THE   SCIP3
0232 *                             OUTPUT TAPE THEN WRITE A TM, TRAILER,   SCIP3
0233 *                             TM.  IT WILL ALSO PRINT THE MESSAGE     SCIP3
0234 *                             BAD OUTPUT ON THE LAST LINE OF THE      SCIP3
0235 *                             EXCEPTION LISTING.                      SCIP3
0236 *                2. IF TAPE INPUT, THE SAME PROCEDURE NOTED FOR       SCIP3
0237 *                   CARD INPUT MAY BE TAKEN EXCEPT FOR MARKING THE    SCIP3
0238 *                   SPOT ON THE INPUT FILE. IT MAY BE WISE TO COUNT   SCIP3
0239 *                   THE NUMBER OF TIMES HALT 600 WAS REACHED.         SCIP3
0240 *     682  W13J5 PROGRAM TRYING TO WRITE TRAILER LABEL ON OUTPUT      SCIP3
0241 *                TAPE 2 BUT ERROR CONDITION PERSISTS.                 SCIP3
0242 *                2 ACTION ALTERNATIVES-                               SCIP3
0243 *                   1. SET SENSE SW G OFF AND PRESS START TO SKIP     SCIP3
0244 *                      AND BLANK TAPE AND TRY AGAIN.                  SCIP3
0245 *                   2. SET SENSE SW G ON AND PRESS START TO BYPASS    SCIP3
0246 *                      TRAILER WRITE AND WRITE 2ND TAPE MARK          SCIP3
0247 *                      INSTEAD.                                       SCIP3
0248 *                      IF THIS ACTION IS TAKEN, THE NEXT PROGRAM      SCIP3
0249 *                      ACUM WILL COME TO HALT 694. IF THE OPERATOR    SCIP3
0250 *                      RUNNING ACUM IS AWARE OF THIS CONDITION HE     SCIP3
0251 *                      WILL BE PREPARED TO TAKE THE PROPER ACTION.    SCIP3
0252 *     800  A02   FIRST CARD NOT A SCIP CONTROL CARD.                  SCIP3
0253 *                RESTART JOB WITH SCIP CONTROL CARD.                  SCIP3
0254 *     999  I21   END OF JOB.                                          SCIP3
0255 *                   LOOK AT LAST LINE OF EXCEPTION LISTING. IF THE    SCIP3
0256 *                   MESSAGE BAD OUTPUT APPEARS THE PROGRAM HAS        SCIP3
0257 *                   DESTROYED THE IMPROPER OUTPUT TAPE DATA AND       SCIP3
0258 *                   THE PROGRAM MUST BE RERUN AFTER ALL OUT OF        SCIP3
0259 *                   SEQUENCE CONDITIONS ARE CORRECTED. SEE HALT       SCIP3
0260 *                   600.                                              SCIP3
0261 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0262 * INPUT - 80 CHARACTER  RECORDS ON  CARDS OR TAPE 1.                  SCIP3
0263 * THERE ARE NO WORD MARKS IN 1 THRU 80.                               SCIP3
0264 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0265 INPUT2    EQU  1                                                      SCIP3
0266 IPID      EQU  8         PROGRAM ID - COLS 1-8.                       SCIP3
0267 IPTYPE    EQU  10        COLS 9-10.                                   SCIP3
0268 IPFCOD    EQU  11        ALWAYS AN ASTERISK                           SCIP3
0269 IPCONT    EQU  12        CONTROL CARD CODES-D I OR M.                 SCIP3
0270 81        DCW  '⯒'       GROUP MARK TO 81.                            SCIP3
0271 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0272 * INPUT - 80 CHARACTER  SCIP PROGRAM CONTROL CARD                     SCIP3
0273 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0274 SCIP      EQU  5         CONTROL CARD IDENTIFICATION, 2-5.            SCIP3
0275 *                        NOTE THAT COL. 1 IS BLANK.                   SCIP3
0276 RPTDTE    EQU  17      REPORT DATE IS MOVED DIRECTLY TO THE REPORT    SCIP3
0277 *                        TITLE LINE AS IS.                            SCIP3
0278 *                        EXAMPLE -   JUN 15, 1964 IN COLS. 6-17.      SCIP3
0279 CREATE    EQU  22      CREATE DATE IS MOVED DIRECTLY TO THE TAPE      SCIP3
0280 *                        HEADER LABEL AREA AS IS.                     SCIP3
0281 *                        FORMAT IS JULIAN DATE YYDDD                  SCIP3
0282 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0283 * COUNTERS, FLAGS, FITTED INTO LOWER MEMORY    ********************   SCIP3
0284 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0285           ORG  82                                                     SCIP3
0286 IPCT      DCW  =5        INPUT RECORD COUNT                           SCIP3
0287           ORG  91                                                     SCIP3
0288 REJECT    DC   =1        FLAG USED BY WRITE OUTPUT ROUTINE TO         SCIP3
0289 *                         REJECT RECORDS. TURNED OFF BY R RTE.        SCIP3
0290 *                         TURNED ON BY B33 AND B39.                   SCIP3
0291           ORG  96                                                     SCIP3
0292 EOJFLG    DCW  =1       IF THIS FLAG DOES NOT CONTAIN A WM IT MEANS   SCIP3
0293 *                        THAT A RUINOUS TYPE OF OUT OF SEQUENCE IN    SCIP3
0294 *                        THE INPUT CAUSED THE OUTPUT TAPE TO BE       SCIP3
0295 *                        USELESS TO THE SYSTEM.                       SCIP3
0296 *                        TURNED ON AT I98B AND INTERROGATED BY END    SCIP3
0297 *                        OF JOB ROUTINE AT I20.                       SCIP3
0298 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0299 *  INDEX REGISTERS                                                    SCIP3
0300 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0301 90        DCW  '000?'   POS 90 IS ABSTRACT CTR USED WITH X1.          SCIP3
0302 95        DCW  '000?'                                                 SCIP3
0303 100       DCW  '000?'                                                 SCIP3
0304 X1        EQU  89   X1 USED TO BUILD ABSTRACT OUTPUT RECORD.          SCIP3
0305 X2        EQU  94     X2 HAS LOCATION OF OUTPUT RCD TO WRITE.         SCIP3
0306 X3        EQU  99        X3 USED BY SUBJECT CODE, SEARCH KEY, AND     SCIP3
0307 *                           PROG MATL MEDIUM CHECKING ROUTINES.       SCIP3
0308 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0309           ORG  101                                                    SCIP3
0310 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0311 * FLAGS USED FOR VALIDITY CHECKING OF INPUT                           SCIP3
0312 * AS EACH CARD IMAGE IS PROCESSED THE CORRESPONDING FLAG IS           SCIP3
0313 *TURNED ON.                                                           SCIP3
0314 * THE FLAGS ARE TURNED OFF WHEN THE RECORD IS WRITTEN OR REJECTED.    SCIP3
0315 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0316           DA   1X10   OFF CODE IS BLANK. ON CODE IS-                  SCIP3
0317 FDEL           1         DELETE PRESENT             D                 SCIP3
0318 FINA           2         INACTIVE PRESENT           I                 SCIP3
0319 FCHA           3         CHANGE PRESENT             M                 SCIP3
0320 FA             4         A-CARD PRESENT             A                 SCIP3
0321 FB             5         B-CARD PRESENT             B                 SCIP3
0322 FC             6         C-CARD PRESENT             C                 SCIP3
0323 FD             7         D-CARD PRESENT             D                 SCIP3
0324 FS             8         S-CARD PRESENT             S                 SCIP3
0325 F0             9         0-CARD PRESENT             0                 SCIP3
0326 FABS           10        ABSTRACT PRESENT           1                 SCIP3
0327 * COMPARE WORD TO CHECK FOR COMPLETE ADDITION PACKAGE.                SCIP3
0328 ADDCK     DCW  'ABCDS01'                                              SCIP3
0329 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0330 PROP      DC   =1        FLAG USED BY P RTE- TURNED OFF AND ON        SCIP3
0331 *                         BY R RTE.                                   SCIP3
0332 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0333 *  OUTPUT HEADER LABEL AREA                                           SCIP3
0334 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0335 HEADR     DCW  1                                                      SCIP3
0336           DCW  'HDR '                                                 SCIP3
0337           DCW  '          -'                                          SCIP3
0338           DCW  '001 '                                                 SCIP3
0339           DCW  'CIR       '                                           SCIP3
0340 DTT       DCW  '     '            YYDDD   YR, DAY 001-366             SCIP3
0341           DCW  '-030 '            RETENTION - NUMBER OF DAYS          SCIP3
0342           DCW  =40                                                    SCIP3
0343           DCW  '⯒'       THIS IS A GROUP MARK.                        SCIP3
0344 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0345 * HOUSEKEEPING                                                        SCIP3
0346 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0347           ORG  200                                                    SCIP3
0348 A01       R                        READ CONTROL CARD.                 SCIP3
0349           SS   2                   SELECT STACKER 2.                  SCIP3
0350           C    5,HEAD1+3       IS IT SCIP CONTROL CARD                SCIP3
0351           BE   A04       YES                                          SCIP3
0352 A02       NOP  800       1ST CARD NOT CONTROL CARD HALT.              SCIP3
0353           H                                                           SCIP3
0354           B    A02                                                    SCIP3
0355 A04       MLC  RPTDTE,HDDATE       MOVE DATE TO REPORT TITLE.         SCIP3
0356           MLC  CREATE,DTT          MOVE CREATE DATE TO HEADER LABEL   SCIP3
0357           B    W10                 BR TO WRITE HEADER LABEL SUB RTE   SCIP3
0357A          CS   10                                                     SCIP3
0358           B    I01                 GET 1ST INPUT RECORD.              SCIP3
0359           MLC  10,PREV             MAKE CURRENT AND PREVIOUS EQUAL    SCIP3
0360 *                                  FOR B03 COMPARE.                   SCIP3
0361           SBR  P99+3,B01      SET PRINT RTE TO RETURN TO B01.         SCIP3
0362 A10       CS   P10,299             CLEAR PRINT AREA AND BRANCH TO     SCIP3
0363 *                             PRINT 1ST REPORT HEADING LINES.         SCIP3
0364           ORG  336                                                    SCIP3
0365 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0366 *  SCIP---SCREEN CARD INPUTS -MAIN ROUTINE                            SCIP3
0367 * THE INSTRUCTION SEGMENT OF THIS PROGRAM STARTS AT 336 INSTEAD       SCIP3
0368 * OF 333 IN ORDER TO TAKE ADVANTAGE OF THE B REGISTER ADDRESS ON      SCIP3
0369 * THE FIRST CS AFTER A PRINT INSTRUCTION ON A 1401 WITHOUT THE        SCIP3
0370 * PRINT STORAGE FEATURE.  IT SAVES A FEW MEMORY POSITIONS.            SCIP3
0371 *******************************************************************   SCIP3
0372 B01       NOP  I01       GET INPUT RECORD - SWITCH - AFTER LAST       SCIP3
0373 *                        INPUT RECORD HAS BEEN READ THIS INST         SCIP3
0374 *                        WILL BE A BR TO I20.                         SCIP3
0375           MLC  LTB,B01       SET B01SW TO BRANCH                      SCIP3
0376 B03       C    8,PREV-2            CHANGE IN PROGRAM I.D.             SCIP3
0377           BU   E01                YES                                 SCIP3
0378 B04       C    10,BLANKS+1         IS IT CONTROL TYPE RECORD.         SCIP3
0379 B04A      BU   B09       AFTER LAST INPUT HAS BEEN READ THIS INST     SCIP3
0380 *                        IS CHANGED TO A BRANCH TO I20.               SCIP3
0381           BCE  F01,12,D           DELETE                              SCIP3
0382           BCE  F08,12,I           INACTIVE                            SCIP3
0383           BCE  F15,12,M           CHANGE HEADER                       SCIP3
0384 B05       SBR  P05+3,MSG4          TYPE CARD UNKNOWN.                 SCIP3
0385           B    P01                 PRINT EXCEPTION.                   SCIP3
0386           B    B01                                                    SCIP3
0387 * A CARD ROUTINE **************************************************   SCIP3
0388 B09       MLC  8,CID          PROG ID TO CHANGE AND ADD OUTPUT AREA   SCIP3
0389           C    10,LTA+1           TYPE A CARD                         SCIP3
0390           BU   B40                NO                                  SCIP3
0391           BCE  B31,FA,A           A CARD PRESENT                      SCIP3
0392 *         EDIT YEAR COMPLETED FOR PR, CH OR NUMERIC.                  SCIP3
0393           C    69,'PR'                                                SCIP3
0394           BE   B20                                                    SCIP3
0395           C    69,'CH'                                                SCIP3
0396           BE   B20                                                    SCIP3
0397           C    69,LTZ              COMPARE TO ZERO TO CHECK FOR       SCIP3
0398           BH   B38                 NUMERIC.                           SCIP3
0399           C    68,LTZ                                                 SCIP3
0400           BH   B38                                                    SCIP3
0401 *         SUBMITTOR S NAME MUST BE PRESENT                            SCIP3
0402 B20       C    38,BLANKS+16                                           SCIP3
0403           BE   B38                                                    SCIP3
0404 *         EDIT ACCESSION OR SDA NUMBER FIELD FOR BLANKS.              SCIP3
0405           BSS  B22,F     THE SENSE SWITCH F OPTION IS TO ALLOW        SCIP3
0406 *                        SUBMITTERS TO PASS THEIR SUBMITTAL CARDS     SCIP3
0407 *                        THRU THE SCIP PROGRAM FOR CHECKING, PRIOR    SCIP3
0408 *                        TO SENDING THEM TO SDA FOR DISTRIBUTION.     SCIP3
0409           BCE  B38,19,                                                SCIP3
0410           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0411           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0412           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0413           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0414           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0415           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0416 *         EDIT PROGRAM I.D. NUMBER - COLS 4, 2,1, MUST BE NON BLANK   SCIP3
0417 B22       BCE  B38,4,                                                 SCIP3
0418           BCE  B38,2,                                                 SCIP3
0419           BCE                                                         SCIP3
0420           MLC  LTA,FA             TURN ON FLAG A                      SCIP3
0421           MLC  69,CYRCMP          MOVE TO RECORD                      SCIP3
0422           B    B01                                                    SCIP3
0423 *                                                                     SCIP3
0424 B31       C    69,CYRCMP           EXACT DUPLICATES                   SCIP3
0425           BE   B01                 YES- IGNORE IT.                    SCIP3
0426 * NON IDENTICAL DUPLICATES                                            SCIP3
0427 B33       SBR  P05+3,MSG2                                             SCIP3
0428           SW   REJECT              SET FLAG TO REJECT PROG ID SET.    SCIP3
0429           B    P01                 PRINT DUPE IN INPUT AREA NOW.      SCIP3
0430           B    B01                                                    SCIP3
0431 *                                                                     SCIP3
0432 B38       MLC  LTA,MSG3-18        INDICATE TYPE OF CARD A             SCIP3
0433 *  X CARD IS IN ERROR ROUTINE                                         SCIP3
0434 B39       SBR  P05+3,MSG3          CARD EDIT FAILED MESSAGE.          SCIP3
0435           SW   REJECT              SET FLAG TO REJECT PROG ID SET.    SCIP3
0436           B    P01                 PRINT ERROR RECORD NOW.            SCIP3
0437           B    B01                                                    SCIP3
0438 * B CARD ROUTINE **************************************************   SCIP3
0439 B40       C    10,LTB+1           TYPE B CARD                         SCIP3
0440           BU   B67                NO                                  SCIP3
0441           BCE  B60,FB,B           B CARD PRESENT                      SCIP3
0442 *         MACHINE TYPE MUST NOT BE BLANK.                             SCIP3
0443           C    64,BLANKS+6                                            SCIP3
0444           BE   B65                                                    SCIP3
0445 *         TYPE OF SUB ROUTINE MUST NOT BE BLANK.                      SCIP3
0446           C    57,BLANKS+1                                            SCIP3
0447           BE   B65                                                    SCIP3
0448 *         PRINCIPAL SOURCE LANGUAGE MUST NOT BE BLANK.                SCIP3
0449           C    48,BLANKS+6                                            SCIP3
0450           BE   B65                                                    SCIP3
0451 * SUBJECT CODE EDIT  - PRIMARY CODE MUST BE PRESENT.                  SCIP3
0452 * SECONDARY CODES NEED NOT BE PRESENT.                                SCIP3
0453 * IF SENSE SWITCH E IS OFF,  THEN THE SHARE RULES APPLY, THAT         SCIP3
0454 * ALL SUBJECT CODES MUST BE ALPHA IN THE FIRST POSITION, NUMERIC      SCIP3
0455 * IN THE SECOND POSITION, AND BLANK IN THE THIRD POSITION.            SCIP3
0456 * IF SENSE SWITCH E IS ON,  THE SUBJECT CODES ARE NOT CHECKED         SCIP3
0457 * EXCEPT FOR THE PRESENCE OF PRIMARY SUBJECT CODE.                    SCIP3
0458           C    29,BLANKS+2     PRIMARY CODE MUST BE NON BLANK.        SCIP3
0459           BE   B65                                                    SCIP3
0460           BSS  B58,E           SWITCH E ON - BY PASS EDITING.         SCIP3
0461           SBR  X3,24              GOING INTO EDIT LOOP                SCIP3
0462 B42       SBR  X3,3+X3             ADD 3 TO X3 CONTENT                SCIP3
0463           C    '042',X3                                               SCIP3
0464           BE   B58                 BR IF ALL THRU CHECKING.           SCIP3
0465           C    2+X3,BLANKS+2       IF SECONDARY CODE MISSING,         SCIP3
0466           BE   B42                 BRANCH TO CHECK NEXT CODE.         SCIP3
0467           BWZ  B65,0+X3,2          ERROR IF NO ZONE-MUST BE ALPHA     SCIP3
0468           BCE  B65,1+X3,           ERROR IF BLANK IN 2ND POS.         SCIP3
0469           BWZ  B43,1+X3,2          2ND. POS MUST BE NUMERIC.          SCIP3
0470           B    B65                                                    SCIP3
